[38;5;231m⏺[39m I've sketched the layout options in a browser tab so they're easier to compare. It should have opened on its own; if
  it didn't, use this link: [94m]8;id=11mt06w;http://localhost:57915/?key=bfc82255a3c9361fa861208931d44db3e79d77e55d5205db6d5f67639e0ac29c\http://localhost:57915/?key=bfc82255a3c9361fa861208931d44db3e79d77e55d5205db6d5f67639e0ac29c]8;;\
[39m  (The companion uses a lot of tokens, so tell me if you'd rather stay in the terminal.)

  All three options group the 12 fields into the same four sections:
  - [1mProfile:[0m display name, email, avatar URL
  - [1mPreferences:[0m time zone, language, theme
  - [1mNotifications:[0m email, push, weekly digest
  - [1mSecurity:[0m two-factor, session timeout, API token

  The options:
  - [1mA. Stacked sections:[0m one page with a heading per group ([38;5;153m<fieldset>[39m/[38;5;153m<legend>[39m) and a single Save button. Only the HTML
    and CSS change, and the form submits exactly what it does today. [1mI recommend this one.[0m
  - [1mB. Tabs:[0m shows one group at a time. It needs tab-switching JavaScript and hides fields you might want to see.
  - [1mC. Sections plus a side nav:[0m A with a sidebar of jump links. It needs a wider container, which is more than 12
    fields call for.

  Which layout do you want? You can click one in the browser, and please also reply here, along with any changes to the
  groupings.

  Note: the companion saves its files in [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/[39m in the repo, which isn't in a [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m yet. I'll leave that
  untracked and won't commit it.

